      "writtenOn": "2023-08-24T20:16:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ohhh, I think we might be talking about different things. In that example, they want to produce one string to give to `print`. In the code here, `[\"ssh\", f\"-p{port}\", host, \"--\"]` is not equivalent to `f\"ssh -p{port} host --\"`.\n\nThe first keeps each str piece as an array element. These array elements are given to `subprocess.run` as separate item, to ensure proper command argument construction.\nThe latter smashes all command line pieces into a single string and then *hopes* that the shell will reinterpret the individual command line items. You typically must run a different function, typically named `shell`, to have a string evaluated for execution.\n\nBad code will smash commands into a single string before execution. We intentionally want to keep each parameter separate, so that we don\u0027t need to deal with escaping and reinterpretation.",
      "parentUuid": "27baaafd_857acaa9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 29,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "37bcc622f33f6842d4229a2e0dbad09d6326d643",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
